python: an extras attribute on the rules that take deps.

Adds `extras` (a list of strings) to python_library, python_binary and
python_test (and the other rules with python_common's deps_arg). The build
ignores it. turnkey's rules sync reads it as the target's variant, the
extras of its package ([project.optional-dependencies]) it is built with,
and adds the dependencies they enable to its deps, as it expands a Rust
target's cargo_features.

--- a/decls/python_common.bzl
+++ b/decls/python_common.bzl
@@ -146,6 +146,15 @@
                 dependencies of these rules.
         """,
         ),
+        "extras": attrs.list(
+            attrs.string(),
+            default = [],
+            doc = """
+            The extras (`[project.optional-dependencies]`) of the target's
+                package it is built with. turnkey's rules sync adds the
+                dependencies they enable to `deps`; the build ignores it.
+        """,
+        ),
     }
 
 def _internal_tools_arg():
